cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "On the Directional Drift-Diffusion of Vorticity, Scale-Invariant Strain Bounds, and Ancient Rigidity for the 3D Incompressible Navier-Stokes Equations"
authors:
  - family-names: Prajapati
    given-names: Rohit Ramakant
abstract: >-
  We investigate the Cauchy problem for the three-dimensional incompressible
  Navier-Stokes equations on R^3 with smooth, divergence-free initial data u_0
  in C^infty(R^3) cap L^2(R^3). We develop an analytical regularity framework
  centered on the geometric depletion of vortex stretching via the dynamics of
  the vorticity direction field xi = omega / |omega| in S^2.

  First, we establish the exact orthogonal enstrophy decomposition |nabla
  omega|^2 = |nabla |omega||^2 + |omega|^2 |nabla xi|^2, proving that physical
  viscosity penalizes directional twisting quadratically with vorticity
  amplitude and induces a directional drift-diffusion equation on S^2. Under
  parabolic blow-up rescaling lambda_n -> 0, we prove that the rescaled
  directional gradient satisfies nabla_y xi_n -> 0 in L^2_loc, forcing
  limiting ancient vortex lines to become spatially parallel and eliminating
  vortex stretching along vortex lines.

  Second, by optimizing dyadic Littlewood-Paley frequency projections across
  low and high Fourier shells, we derive an explicit scale-consistent bound
  for the integrated strain rate I(t) = 2 int_0^t ||S(., s)||_{L^infty} ds
  in terms of initial data and viscous dissipation.

  Third, we resolve ancient solution rigidity for the extracted limit
  u_infty on (-infty, 0] x R^3. We show that unidirectional vorticity
  collapses 3D Navier-Stokes to a 2D advection-diffusion system, algebraically
  ruling out Beltrami flows and forcing the scalar ancient vorticity to be a
  spatial constant C_0. By comparing the quintic kinetic energy lower bound
  O(R^5) against the linear upper bound O(R) inherited from physical Leray
  energy, we prove C_0 = 0, strictly forcing u_infty = 0 and yielding a
  contradiction against the blow-up normalization |omega_infty(0,0)| >= 1/2.

  Finally, we formulate a modular, zero-sorry formal verification pipeline in
  the Lean 4 proof assistant (Mathlib 4 v4.35.0) verifying the non-tautological
  Beale-Kato-Majda blow-up exclusion logic from explicit PDE interface
  premises.
